<report>
<title>Contingency table analysis</title>
<table>
<block name="rows">
<tr><td>Observed</td><block name="obs"><td>@{obs:roundu}</td></block><td><subtotal><block name="rtot">@{rtot:roundu}</block></subtotal></td><td><block name="score"><score>@{score:roundu}</score></block></td></tr>
<block name="exps"><tr><td><model>Expected</model></td><block name="exp"><td><model>@{exp:roundu}</model></td></block><td></td><td></td></tr></block>
<block name="chis"><tr><td>DChi&#xb2;</td><block name="chi"><td>@{chi:roundu}</td></block><td></td><td></td></tr></block>
<block name="pcrs">
<tr><td>% of row</td><block name="pcr"><td>@{pcr:round2}%</td></block><td></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>% of col</td><block name="pcc"><td>@{pcc:round2}%</td></block><td></td></tr>
</block>
<tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
</block>
<tr><td><subtotal><b>Total</b></subtotal></td><block name="tot"><td><subtotal><b>@{tot:roundu}</b></subtotal></td></block><td></td></tr>
<block name="pcgs"><tr><td>% of n</td><block name="pcg"><td>@{pcg:round2}%</td></block><td></td><td></td></tr></block>
<block name="scores"><tr><td></td><block name="score"><td><score>@score</score></td></block><td></td><td></td></tr></block>
</table>

<p>TOTAL number of cells = @tot</p>
<block name="warn">

<p><warn>@warn</warn></p>
</block>
<subtitle>NOMINAL INDEPENDENCE</subtitle>
<table>
<tr><td>Chi-square = @{chio:roundu}</td><td>DF = @{dfo:roundu}</td><td><pval>@{po:pval}<block name="pmcx2">  Monte Carlo @{p:pval} (@{pc:round2}% CI: @{ll:roundu} to @{ul:roundu}@warn; iterations: @its; seed: @seed)</block>
</pval></td></tr>
<tr><td>G-square = @{g2:roundu}</td><td>DF = @{dfo:roundu}</td><td><pval>@{pog2:pval}<block name="pmcg2">  Monte Carlo @{p:pval} (@{pc:round2}% CI: @{ll:roundu} to @{ul:roundu}@warn; iterations: @its; seed: @seed)</block>
</pval></td></tr>
<tr><td>Fisher-Freeman-Halton exact</td><td></td><td><pval>@{p2:pval}</pval>  @lb</td></tr>
</table>
<subtitle>ANOVA</subtitle>
<p>Chi-square for equality of mean column scores = @{chie:roundu}<br />
DF = @dfe <pval>@{pe:pval}<block name="pmcx2eq">  Monte Carlo @{p:pval} (@{pc:round2}% CI: @{ll:roundu} to @{ul:roundu}@warn; iterations: @its; seed: @seed)</block>
</pval></p>

<subtitle>LINEAR TREND</subtitle>
<p>Sample correlation (r) = @{r:roundu}<br />
Chi-square for linear trend (M&#xb2;) = @{chit:roundu}<br />
DF = 1  <pval>@{pt:pval}<block name="pmcx2trend">  Monte Carlo @{p:pval} (@{pc:round2}% CI: @{ll:roundu} to @{ul:roundu}@warn; iterations: @its; seed: @seed)</block>
</pval></p>

<subtitle>NOMINAL ASSOCIATION</subtitle>
<p>Phi = @{phi:roundu}<br />
Pearson's contingency = @{pearson:roundu}<br />
Cram&#xe9;r's <i>V</i> = @{cramer:roundu}@cramernote</p>

<subtitle>ORDINAL</subtitle>
<p>Goodman-Kruskal gamma = @{gamma:roundu}</p>
<table>
<tr><td>Approximate test of gamma = 0:</td><td>SE = @{seg:roundu}</td><td><pval>@{pg:pval}</pval></td><td><ci>@{pc:round2}% CI = @{llg:roundu} to @{ulg:roundu}</ci></td></tr>
<tr><td>Approximate test of independence:</td><td>SE = @{segi:roundu}</td><td><pval>@{pgi:pval}</pval></td><td><ci>@{pc:round2}% CI = @{llgi:roundu} to @{ulgi:roundu}</ci></td></tr>
</table>

<p>Kendall tau-b = @{taub:roundu}</p>
<table>
<tr><td>Approximate test of tau-b = 0:</td><td>SE = @{setaub:roundu}</td><td><pval>@{ptaub:pval}</pval></td><td><ci>@{pc:round2}% CI = @{lltaub:roundu} to @{ultaub:roundu}</ci></td></tr>
<tr><td>Approximate test of independence:</td><td>SE = @{setaubi:roundu}</td><td><pval>@{ptaubi:pval}</pval></td><td><ci>@{pc:round2}% CI = @{lltaubi:roundu} to @{ultaubi:roundu}</ci></td></tr>
</table>
</report>
